(EXP-73: a text made from a buffer is an independent copy, not a
 window - it keeps its own bytes after the buffer that made it is
 cleared and refilled (LANGUAGE.md:2051-2057). This is the memory-safety
 row of the whole section, per the ledger's own Report ("the manual's
 own stated reason is that a window would read freed memory after a
 resize") - CLAUDE.md's priority ordering put it first in this batch.
 The capture happens BEFORE the mutation and the assertion runs AFTER
 it, so the check actually exercises independence rather than a text
 trivially equalling itself; a second capture+check right after proves
 the buffer's own later state is unaffected by the fact that an earlier
 copy was taken. Content is built from 'gen expr safe text' (letters and
 digits only - see that helper's own comment) so it drops straight into
 a double-quoted buffer-content literal with no escaping question.)

