(EXP-83, EXP-84: base-conversion parsing stops at the first character
 invalid for the chosen base rather than raising (LANGUAGE.md:2116-2118,
 the manual's own `"12g5" as a hex number` -> 18), and a numeral invalid
 from its very first character gives 0 (LANGUAGE.md:2118-2120) - the
 real gap `'gen leaf base conversion'` (gen_text.vox) never reaches,
 since every digit it emits is drawn from the chosen base's own
 alphabet on purpose. Neither row touches the D2 discrepancy (still
 open, blocked) - that one is about the ERROR FLAG; these two are about
 the VALUE, which both bullets agree on and hand-verification confirms.
 Base is drawn 2-35, never 36 (base 36 already spans the whole 0-9a-z
 alphabet, so no invalid digit would exist to append). The partial-parse
 half also appends one further trailing character after the invalid
 one, the same "g5" shape the manual's own example uses, to show
 parsing really stops rather than merely ending. The total-failure half
 sometimes draws the empty string instead (LANGUAGE.md's own `""` case,
 hand-verified 0 across four parse-form spellings including two
 non-default bases) rather than a string with an invalid first
 character - both are "zero characters consumed".)

